<title>australia: RTRS-Australia July housing finance rises 16.0 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia July housing finance rises 16.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance commitments for owner-occupied housing in Australia rose 16.0 percent by volume to 40,483 dwellings in July, seasonally-adjusted, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In value terms, housing finance rose to A$4.01 billion in July from A$3.42 billion in June, the bureau said.</p>
<p>Analysts forecasts had centered on a 4.7 percent rise in commitments for July.  </p>
<p>Australian housing finance, July 1996 -</p>
<p>    Dwelling commitments     July 96    June 96     July 95</p>
<p>    Seasonally-adjusted	 40,483     34,894	37,536</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		    42,654     35,465	36,825</p>
<p>    Trend			   37,419     37,534	36,264</p>
<p>Value (A$ billion)</p>
<p>    Seasonally-adjusted	  4.01	 3.42	  3.63</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		     4.22	 3.49	  3.57</p>
<p>    Trend estimates		3.68	 3.68	  3.49</p>
<p>The Bureau said financing by banks rose 19.1 percent in July, while financing by building societies rose 3.1 percent and other lenders rose 1.8 percent, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>The bureau said the jump in July was the result of significant increases in refinancing of existing loans which were up almost 25 percent and commitments for purchase of established dwellings which rose 15.0 percent.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
